<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Highline Cutoff Trail (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:148-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:trillium-lake-sno-park (OSM parking way/148019331); confidence: high; pdf_page: 150; book_elev_ft: 3830</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270371" lon="-121.732742"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Campground junction</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Trillium Lake Road and Trillium Lake Loop Road (NF 2656), node 37397443, east of the lake by the campground; confidence: high; pdf_page: 146; quote: From the campground junction east of Trillium Lake (see map) take the road angling uphill for a long, gentle climb to the Jefferson Viewpoint</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247437" lon="-121.738521"><ele>1193.3</ele><name>Jefferson Viewpoint</name><desc>source: OSM Trillium Lake Loop Road node 37598739, 1.79 mi from the campground junction (osm_lookup along), at the road's sweeping turn east; DEM 3,915 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 146; book_elev_ft: 3940; quote: 1.8 miles from the junction and 3.5 miles from the sno-park ... The road makes a sweeping turn at the viewpoint</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.243053" lon="-121.733122"><ele>1211.2</ele><name>High Divide (Lostman Trail junction)</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Trillium Lake Loop Road and Lost Man Trail, node 2452534627; DEM 3,974 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; book_elev_ft: 4040; quote: Follow the Mud Creek Ridge road 0.6 mile beyond the Jefferson Viewpoint to the High Divide ... Here, the Lostman Trail is the obvious side road to the left (east).</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.229466" lon="-121.744614"><ele>1133.2</ele><name>Big Bend</name><desc>source: OSM Trillium Lake Loop Road node 2452545085, the loop's southern tip where the High Divide road turns north as the Lower Ridge road; confidence: high; pdf_page: 147</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.231206" lon="-121.748168"><ele>1121.3</ele><name>Side road west (on Loop Road)</name><desc>source: OSM Trillium Lake Loop Road node 37598919, nearest to the east end of unnamed OSM track way/238032538 (15 m gap); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; quote: Just west of Big Bend look for a side road to the west along the bottom of a clearcut. This road leads to Asgard Meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.231150" lon="-121.748360"><ele>1121.0</ele><name>Side road start</name><desc>source: OSM node 2459019637, east end of track way/238032538; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.228995" lon="-121.759334"><ele>1095.2</ele><name>Highline Cutoff spur leaves the side road</name><desc>source: OSM node 2452545242, where unnamed track way/237337444 leaves the Asgard Meadow side road (way/238032538) north, before the side road's curve; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; quote: turn right where it starts to curve and take another side road and go right (north) into big timber. Go 200 yards and exit the old growth onto the Highline Cutoff</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.232833" lon="-121.765246"><ele>1055.1</ele><name>Highline Cutoff bench (spur end)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2452545201, west end of way/237337444 after it turns left (west) and curves along the bench above Mud Creek; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; quote: Turn left then curve northward on this bench overlooking the Mud Creek valley and the Salmon River road below.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.233654" lon="-121.765824"><ele>1023.4</ele><name>Salmon River road</name><desc>source: OSM Forest Road 309 (way/238035234) node 37418969, nearest to the spur end (about 100 m); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; quote: Descend to Salmon River road and turn right to return to the Trillium Lake area</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247059" lon="-121.752229"><ele>1068.7</ele><name>Salmon River road leaves the Lower Ridge road</name><desc>source: OSM node where Forest Road 309 (way/238035234, the Salmon River road) leaves Trillium Lake Loop Road; DEM 3,506 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 151; quote: the best direction continues on the Lower Ridge road, then branches off onto the Salmon River road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270371" lon="-121.732742"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Campground junction (return)</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Trillium Lake Road and Trillium Lake Loop Road (NF 2656), as 150-2; confidence: high; pdf_page: 147</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Highline Cutoff Trail (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Trillium Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Campground junction: osm (high), 1.33 mi | 2. Campground junction -&gt; Jefferson Viewpoint: osm (high), 1.79 mi | 3. Jefferson Viewpoint -&gt; High Divide (Lostman Trail junction): osm (high), 0.55 mi | 4. High Divide (Lostman Trail junction) -&gt; Big Bend: osm (high), 1.13 mi | 5. Big Bend -&gt; Side road west (on Loop Road): osm (high), 0.25 mi | 6. Side road west (on Loop Road) -&gt; Side road start: straight (medium), 0.01 mi | 7. Side road start -&gt; Highline Cutoff spur leaves the side road: osm (medium), 0.58 mi | 8. Highline Cutoff spur leaves the side road -&gt; Highline Cutoff bench (spur end): osm (medium), 0.55 mi | 9. Highline Cutoff bench (spur end) -&gt; Salmon River road: straight (low), 0.06 mi | 10. Salmon River road -&gt; Salmon River road leaves the Lower Ridge road: osm (high), 1.33 mi | 11. Salmon River road leaves the Lower Ridge road -&gt; Campground junction (return): osm (high), 2.23 mi | 12. Campground junction (return) -&gt; Trillium Lake Sno-Park (finish): osm (high), 1.33 mi</desc>
